    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah typically cover sudden and accidental hail damage to your roof, siding, and physical structure under dwelling coverage."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\u26a0\ufe0f Watch Out for Separate Deductibles"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Percentage-based costs: Many Utah policies use a separate wind and hail deductible instead of a flat fee."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insured home value: This is calculated as 1% to 2% (or more) of your dwelling coverage limit, not the repair bill."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Out-of-pocket math: On a $400,000 insured home, a 2% hail deductible means you pay the first $8,000 before insurance pays anything."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udca1 What is Typically Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof & Exterior: Shingles, vents, gutters, and siding beaten up by ice stones."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Other Structures: Detached garages, sheds, or fences on your property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Personal Property: Belongings inside if a hole in the roof lets water or a fallen tree ruin them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udd0e Key Policy Factors to Check"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "RCV vs. ACV: Replacement Cost Value (RCV) pays for a new roof, while Actual Cash Value (ACV) subtracts heavy depreciation for an older roof's age."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cosmetic Exclusions: Some modern policies exclude purely cosmetic dents on metal roofs or siding if functionality isn't lost."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Age: Insurers may refuse full payouts or bump up requirements if an asphalt shingle roof is past its normal lifespan."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Read a helpful overview of local considerations from Homeowners Insurance in Utah Valley .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Homeowners Insurance in Utah Valley",
                "link": "https://provo.com/living/homeowners-insurance-utah-valley/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review state-specific consumer guidelines via the Utah Insurance Department .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/disaster-preparedness/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Understand percentage calculations with tips from Country Financial .\n</To Learn More>",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Country Financial",
                "link": "https://www.countryfinancial.com/en/planning/common-topics/insurance-coverage/calculate-homeowners-insurance-deductible.html"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your approximate dwelling coverage limit or roof age, I can help you calculate your exact estimated out-of-pocket hail deductible."
      }
    ],
